Subject: Serialize RecordDecl's HasUnion bit in precompiled headers and modules
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

Fil-C's clang marks stack temporaries of records that contain a union with
zhas_union, which keeps SROA from splitting them, keyed on
RecordDecl::HasUnion. Sema sets that bit, but ASTWriter did not write it,
so every record read
from a PCH or module (std::string included) lost it. Since 0.686 lowers
pointer-bearing unions to pointer words, SROA then split a std::string
temporary and turned the copy of a string literal into a misaligned pointer
load, which traps: Nix's unit tests, built with a meson PCH, failed in
global constructors. Applied to filc0 for every Fil-C variant; the
regression check is checks.pch-union (tests/pch-union.nix).

The C record abbreviation's packed-bits field grows to 15 bits: 20.1.8
already packed 14 bits into its 13-bit field, so a C record that can never
be passed in registers would have been written incorrectly.

From eaa5947bfd9e1368b64927d7407f84fdcab2ee94 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:46:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Serialize RecordDecl's HasUnion bit in precompiled
 headers and modules

Amp-Thread-ID: https://ampcode.com/threads/T-01a1a83f-db70-70ea-9a7b-2baced9ee25c
Co-authored-by: Amp <amp@ampcode.com>
---
 clang/lib/Serialization/ASTReaderDecl.cpp | 1 +
 clang/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterDecl.cpp | 5 +++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTReaderDecl.cpp b/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTReaderDecl.cpp
index b4ff71c8958a..7fb133040c99 100644
--- a/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTReaderDecl.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTReaderDecl.cpp
@@ -835,6 +835,7 @@ RedeclarableResult ASTDeclReader::VisitRecordDeclImpl(RecordDecl *RD) {
       RecordDeclBits.getNextBit());
   RD->setHasNonTrivialToPrimitiveDestructCUnion(RecordDeclBits.getNextBit());
   RD->setHasNonTrivialToPrimitiveCopyCUnion(RecordDeclBits.getNextBit());
+  RD->setHasUnion(RecordDeclBits.getNextBit());
   RD->setHasUninitializedExplicitInitFields(RecordDeclBits.getNextBit());
   RD->setParamDestroyedInCallee(RecordDeclBits.getNextBit());
   RD->setArgPassingRestrictions(
diff --git a/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterDecl.cpp b/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterDecl.cpp
index a5d8a3f05bc9..ddb36690bf70 100644
--- a/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterDecl.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Serialization/ASTWriterDecl.cpp
@@ -626,6 +626,7 @@ void ASTDeclWriter::VisitRecordDecl(RecordDecl *D) {
   RecordDeclBits.addBit(D->hasNonTrivialToPrimitiveDefaultInitializeCUnion());
   RecordDeclBits.addBit(D->hasNonTrivialToPrimitiveDestructCUnion());
   RecordDeclBits.addBit(D->hasNonTrivialToPrimitiveCopyCUnion());
+  RecordDeclBits.addBit(D->hasUnion());
   RecordDeclBits.addBit(D->hasUninitializedExplicitInitFields());
   RecordDeclBits.addBit(D->isParamDestroyedInCallee());
   RecordDeclBits.addBits(llvm::to_underlying(D->getArgPassingRestrictions()), 2);
@@ -2513,13 +2514,13 @@ void ASTWriter::WriteDeclAbbrevs() {
   // RecordDecl
   Abv->Add(BitCodeAbbrevOp(
       BitCodeAbbrevOp::Fixed,
-      13)); // Packed Record Decl Bits: FlexibleArrayMember,
+      15)); // Packed Record Decl Bits: FlexibleArrayMember,
             // AnonymousStructUnion, hasObjectMember, hasVolatileMember,
             // isNonTrivialToPrimitiveDefaultInitialize,
             // isNonTrivialToPrimitiveCopy, isNonTrivialToPrimitiveDestroy,
             // hasNonTrivialToPrimitiveDefaultInitializeCUnion,
             // hasNonTrivialToPrimitiveDestructCUnion,
-            // hasNonTrivialToPrimitiveCopyCUnion,
+            // hasNonTrivialToPrimitiveCopyCUnion, hasUnion,
             // hasUninitializedExplicitInitFields, isParamDestroyedInCallee,
             // getArgPassingRestrictions
   // ODRHash
